# Test Conventions (TypeScript)

Apply when editing `tests/**/*.ts`. Read [doc/stack.md](../../doc/stack.md). Subagent: `test-agent`.

## What tests document

Test code explains **What** — behavior, inputs, expected outcome. Use descriptive names.

## Naming

Full rules: [doc/coding-conventions.md](../../doc/coding-conventions.md), patterns: [test-code-patterns.md](../../.cursor/skills/spec-test-design/references/test-code-patterns.md).

| Target | Convention | Example |
|--------|------------|---------|
| Test files | kebab-case + `.test.ts` | `user-service.test.ts` |
| `describe` / `it` | TC ID + What | `'TC-001: returns 404 when item missing'` |

- Include TC ID from `doc/testspec-*.md`
- Name expected outcome, not implementation (`returns 404` not `calls kv.get`)

## Layout

- Tests under paths in `test_roots` from `doc/stack.md`
- Mirror source module paths when practical
- Do not place tests under production source dirs

## Determinism

- Mock I/O, network, time, randomness per stack notes in `doc/stack.md`
- No live external services in unit tests
- Follow [test-code-patterns.md](../../.cursor/skills/spec-test-design/references/test-code-patterns.md) when using Vitest

## Testspec alignment

- TC IDs must match `doc/testspec-*.md`
- New behavior: testspec before or with test code

## Commands

Use `test_single` / `test_all` from `doc/stack.md`.
